{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_94087de7968fa52ee400f4220960acc27f0def0c5ab66fb77249e457e6c49abd", "title": "Jim Ward (musician)", "text": "James David Ward (born September 19, 1976) is an American musician. A self-taught guitarist and pianist, he is the lead singer and rhythm guitarist for the band Sparta; he is also a co-founder of the post-hardcore band At the Drive-In, which he formed in 1993 when he was 17 years old.", "score": 23.0696}, {"id": "hp_doc_1bf3c568411a251dd6e5dd8e44799bdd852ac6f874337bdbd5156c5d2bf7b140", "title": "Quiet (EP)", "text": "Quiet is a solo EP released by Jim Ward. It is the first time Ward has released an album of solo material, although he has previously released two solo songs on compilation discs. It was released November 6, 2007 by Ward's own Civil Defense League record label. The album was marketed and distributed by Doghouse Records.", "score": 14.2029}, {"id": "hp_doc_34964772e5f97d69c579849b2afd238a0a6d8b0d0fb8c1932ad853d3f368a384", "title": "Sparta (band)", "text": "Sparta is an American rock band from El Paso, Texas, formed in 2001. Founding members Jim Ward (vocalist/guitarist) and Tony Hajjar (drummer) are also members of post-hardcore group At the Drive-In. Keeley Davis (guitarist) is the former frontman of Engine Down.", "score": 12.8339}], "remaining_searches": 2}
